<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tan Date</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">late 17th century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tan Date was the leader under whom <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bono-people">Abron</a> (Bono) migrants moved west in the late 17th century, escaping the rising power of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashanti-empire">Ashanti Empire</a>, and settled around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bondoukou">Bondoukou</a> on the border of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana">Ghana</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-coast">Ivory Coast</a>. Abron tradition remembers him as the founder and first king of Gyaman, which grew rich on the trade of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wangara">Dyula</a> merchants there.</p></div>
